      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `Base16.decode()` throws `IllegalArgumentException` when the input contains a non-hex character (`'S'`, ASCII 83). Let me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version adds a descriptive Javadoc comment explaining why the input is invalid (character `'S'` at ASCII 83 is not in the Base16 alphabet), renames the local variable to `inputWithInvalidHexCharacter` for clarity, and adds an inline comment in the catch block to reinforce the expected failure reason — all without changing the runtime behaviour."
